From 0c867559df7295e0c58bf8426fb5342bab5a052b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francis Poulin <fpoulin@uwaterloo.ca>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:27:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] NetInflow: one target shared by GravityWaveRadiation
 sides, pinning their net inflow

A target_transport = NetInflow(Q) on several GravityWaveRadiation sides pins their net inflow,
counted positive into the domain, to Q: after the Flather fill of every barotropic substep, one
uniform shift common to those sides (with the sign of each side's inflow) lands the sum exactly on
Q, as the volume constraints of NEMO (ln_vol) and ROMS (VolCons) do. Unlike a per-side target, the
split of the inflow between the sides is left to the Flather condition.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Abhhvq1qCGMUttoPHbe9Mr
